add('CAP01','Saab sales governance exists, but trigger is internally inconsistent',['CG001'],'pp31,60,70,124–126,131','Saab AB (publ); business areas and Group Ethics and Compliance Board','Sweden','B,F','1,3','Annual report describes screening all new opportunities, deeper due diligence, business-area decisions and potential escalation. GC Annika Bäremo is named p60. Collective management Ethics and Compliance Board has responsible-sales decision remit p70; corporate Board of Directors receives outcomes. p126 requires reassessment if material information emerges and assessment no older than twelve months at sales closure. Reported eight assessments in 2025.','p31/124 use conjunctive triggers; p126 accounting principles use any/or. Cannot choose stronger wording. Eight assessments are not eight refusals or eight weapon-release approvals. GC membership is not personal veto. Export IHL assessment p131 refers to ISP government criteria. No named autonomy sale conditioned or refused.','flagged if any of the following criteria are met','Operative Responsible Sales Policy, CRM flag logic, delegated authority matrix and anonymized decision/conditions.')
